Speak with the app's own display name: no "Tolkara" in text a person reads.

Brighter Pocket's players never see Tolkara's name: the app is Brighter Pocket on their home
screen, and its library title, notices, alerts, execution-mode texts and diagnostics should say
the same. TKAppDisplayName() (launcher/App/ExecutionMode.h) returns the bundle's
CFBundleDisplayName, else CFBundleName, else "Tolkara", which is Tolkara's own name on Tolkara's
own build; every user-facing string that named Tolkara now formats that name in, including the
Files app path to the app's folder (Files shows the Documents folder under the display name).
The microphone usage text names no app, and an unavailable execution mode says only "Not included
in this build." without naming a build target. Keys, identifiers, folder names on disk
and log lines are unchanged.

Upstream candidate: brand-free, the strings follow whatever name the bundle is given, and on
Tolkara's own build they read as before.

